PebbleOS fork
-------------

This is the uPNG used by PebbleOS. It differs from upstream in:

- APNG support (iterative frame decoding) and PNG8 alpha palettes;
- decoding into the image's own format, from an in-memory buffer or, with
  upng_load_stream(), with the compressed data read from storage through a
  callback so it is never resident beside the decoded image;
- inflate through uzlib (https://github.com/pfalcon/uzlib), which must be
  on the include path and linked in;
- allocation through UPNG_MALLOC() and UPNG_FREE(), malloc() and free()
  unless UPNG_CONFIG_FILE names a header that defines them;
- validation of chunk sizes, frame geometry and image dimensions against
  malformed input.

See upng.h for the API.
